This is a very common error when working with the MUI X Date Pickers. MUI requires a localization context to know which date library you are using (in your case, dayjs) so it can format the dates correctly.
To fix this, you need to import the LocalizationProvider and the AdapterDayjs, and then wrap your DateTimePicker inside it.
Here is exactly how to update your code:
### 1. Add the missing imports at the top of your file
Add these two lines right next to your existing DateTimePicker and dayjs imports:
```javascript
import { LocalizationProvider } from "@mui/x-date-pickers/LocalizationProvider";
import { AdapterDayjs } from "@mui/x-date-pickers/AdapterDayjs";

```
### 2. Wrap the Date Picker in the Provider
Find the scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" block inside your JSX and wrap the Box containing the date picker with the <LocalizationProvider dateAdapter={AdapterDayjs}> component:
```jsx
{scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" && (
  <LocalizationProvider dateAdapter={AdapterDayjs}>
    <Box
      sx={{
        mt: 2,
        mb: 2,
        p: 3,
        borderRadius: 2,
        border: "1px solid",
        borderColor: "divider",
        animation: "fadeIn 0.2s ease-in-out",
        backgroundColor: "white",
      }}
    >
      <DateTimePicker
        label="New Execution Date & Time"
        value={finalScheduleTime ? dayjs(finalScheduleTime) : null}
        onChange={(newValue) => {
          setFinalScheduleTime(newValue ? newValue.format("YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm") : "");
        }}
        minDateTime={dayjs().add(30, 'minute')}
        maxDateTime={dayjs().add(24, 'hour')}
        timeSteps={{ minutes: 1 }}
        slotProps={{
          textField: {
            size: 'small',
            fullWidth: true,
            required: true,
            sx: { caretColor: 'transparent' },
            helperText: "Scheduling is only allowed between 30 minutes and 24 hours from current time.",
            onKeyDown: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
            onPaste: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
            inputProps: { readOnly: true } 
          }
        }}
      />
    </Box>
  </LocalizationProvider>
)}

```
By wrapping the specific component block with the LocalizationProvider and passing it AdapterDayjs, the DateTimePicker will successfully boot up without throwing the crash error.
